The file /yolo/models/risk_seq_model.pth is a binary file that contains the trained weights for the risk sequence model. As such, it cannot be represented as text content. You would typically generate this file by training the model defined in src/models/risk_seq_model.py and saving the model's state_dict using PyTorch's `torch.save()` function.

If you need to create this file, you would first need to run the training script that utilizes the RiskSequenceModel class and save the model weights to this path. 

For now, I will leave this file intentionally blank as it is not meant to contain text content. 

